WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.196
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.196 --> 00:00:15.101
The last basic episode: checking your own world, so you find the mistakes before your players do.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.841
I broke something on purpose: a trait that hands out a Golden Whistle, and there's no such item.

6
00:00:22.841 --> 00:00:23.841
Studio notices.

7
00:00:23.841 --> 00:00:27.077
The warning button, bottom right, opens this bar,

8
00:00:27.077 --> 00:00:30.908
and it says exactly what's wrong and which items do exist.

9
00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:36.608
The link at the end takes you straight to the problem: the trait, at its starting items.

10
00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:38.693
Fix it there, and the warning goes.

11
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.626
Then names. I ran the name checker from my update special on the Workshop,

12
00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:46.706
and it found one in our own world.

13
00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:51.895
The quest and the story start were both called The Lion's Gone Walkabout,

14
00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:53.773
so one of them had to change.

15
00:00:54.233 --> 00:01:00.561
I renamed the story start to First Morning in Mudbury, and the checker comes back clean.

16
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:07.201
The version button up top shows the engine version your world needs,

17
00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:12.653
and where players can play it: production, beta and alpha.

18
00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:15.397
All three can play our latest edits.

19
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.629
Size limits catch people out.

20
00:01:18.629 --> 00:01:22.098
A draft is checked at one and a half times every limit,

21
00:01:22.098 --> 00:01:25.188
so it can hold more than it's allowed to publish.

22
00:01:25.188 --> 00:01:29.729
Publishing enforces the real numbers, so trim it before you hit publish.

23
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.270
And last, play it.

24
00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:36.565
Save and Play, in the menu beside Save, starts a game on your draft.

25
00:01:36.565 --> 00:01:38.902
Play every story start once yourself,

26
00:01:38.902 --> 00:01:43.324
because a mistake that never shows as a warning still shows in a game.

27
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:46.485
And that's the basics done.

28
00:01:46.485 --> 00:01:50.443
The Workshop world is built end to end, every part on camera.

29
00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:56.413
Next comes the advanced series, where we dig into the complex stuff I ship in my own worlds.

30
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:00.815
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

